  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving livelihoods through the production and marketing of cacao in the province of Bocas del Toro</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ngbe culture in the Panamanian province of Bocas de Toro live in extreme poverty and are a socially marginalized group. APROTENG-B works with 58 indigenous Ngbe families to strengthen their cacao cooperative, Cooperative de Servicios Multiples Ngbe-Cmaco, R.L. This support is helping to improve cacao production, increase family income, and bolster civil society. Through workshops, farmer-to-farmer exchanges, and youth promoter training, project participants build skills in cacao production, post-harvest management, and leadership and teamwork. The project benefits 64 producers directly and about 385 persons indirectly. APROTENG-B&apos;s activities contribute to expanded economic opportunity in Panama by supporting sustainable smallholder agriculture, local entrepreneurship, and market development.</narrative>
  </description>
